post_install() {
	cat <<'EOF'

  Start with:

      ferestre doctor      what this machine is missing, in order
      ferestre help        the subcommands

  Two things it will almost certainly tell you:

    * Point the tools at the packaged runtime, once:

          export XODUS_PROTON_DIR=/usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d/ferestre

    * Sign in with your own Microsoft account before anything can be
      downloaded:

          xodus-cli login

      Tokens go to the desktop keyring over the Secret Service D-Bus
      interface. Without a keyring provider running, sign-in aborts rather
      than degrading.

  You need to own the titles. This installs no game content and cannot get
  you any: it downloads your purchases with your licence.

  The launch scripts live in /usr/lib/ferestre/scripts and take every path from
  XODUS_* environment variables -- `ferestre env` prints what they resolve to.
  /usr/share/doc/ferestre/RECIPES.md is the per-title walkthrough.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
	post_install
}
